tip: | Look at the house. | A handful of colors from DB16, and no black line anywhere. Everything is on three small ramps.
tip: 5 | Sel-out. | The outline is not one color. Each outline pixel is a step darker than the art beside it: orange by the walls, deep blue by the roof. The house sits softly on any background.
tip: | Try it. | Tap the wall, the door and the chimney with the Color picker. They are all steps on one Oranges ramp. Reusing colors is what a limited palette means. | picker
